    "title": "Denied! Tory Lanez's Appeal REJECTED by Judge, Star Must Serve 10-Year Prison Term for Megan Thee Stallion Shooting - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Malik Davis ,\n6 hours ago\nTory Lanez will remain behind bars at least for now.\nFull story below...\nThe California Court of Appeals upheld the rapper’s felony convictions and 10-year prison sentence for the 2020 shooting of Megan Thee Stallion , according to legal journalist Meghann Cuniff.\nMegan’s attorney, Alex Spiro , released a 31-page response refuting renewed efforts by Lanez’s legal team and supporters to challenge the conviction.\nThe report also reaffirmed that Ring camera footage had been introduced during the trial and that DNA evidence from the firearm showed a high percentage that the shooter was male.\nSpiro shared:\n“Despite Mr. Lanez being convicted at trial by overwhelming evidence that included his own admission of guilt, he and his team, flanked by any ignorant person they can find, have pushed whatever misleading narrative they can.”\nThat’s not all.\nAs previously reported , a judge also denied Lanez’s request to avoid testifying in a related civil case.\nThe deposition is related to Megan Thee Stallion's defamation case against gossip blogger Milagro Gramz, who she claims circulated misleading information about the incident and the 2022 trial, reportedly with Lanez's financial support.\nTory Lanez is set to be released from prison in 2033.\nYour thoughts? 76",
